    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d378">

                <pb facs="0360" n="350" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg350"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.51/1192: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-06T12:00:00-03:00">November 6,
                        1937—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received November 6—11:57 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>141. Boucas<anchor n="40" xml:id="d378-f1"/> informs me that on account of the
                    present confused situation caused by the decision of the Government to alter its
                    coffee policy the Minister of Finance<anchor n="41" xml:id="d378-f2"/> is
                    considering recommending a suspension of service on certain foreign debts. He
                    asserted, however, <pb facs="0361" n="351" xml:id="pg351"/> that both the
                    Minister of Finance and himself are determined to protect the dollar bonds in
                    accordance with the conversations held in Washington.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d378-f1" n="40" xml:id="d378-f1-content">
                <p>Valentim Bouças, member of the Brazilian Federal Foreign Trade Council and
                    Special Technical Adviser to the Minister for Finance.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d378-f2" n="41" xml:id="d378-f2-content">
                <p>Arthur de Souza Costa.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
